Let's outline the key steps: \[
\displaystyle 
\prod_{k=1}^{\infty}\frac{\sin\!\left(\dfrac{\pi}{2^{k}}\right)}
{3\,\sin\!\left(\dfrac{\pi}{3\cdot2^{k}}\right)}
\;=\;
\lim_{N\to\infty}
\frac{\displaystyle\prod_{k=1}^{N}\sin\!\left(\frac{\pi}{2^{k}}\right)}
{3^{\,N}\displaystyle\prod_{k=1}^{N}\sin\!\left(\frac{\pi}{3\cdot2^{k}}\right)}
\]

Using Viète’s formula  

\[
\sin x = x\prod_{n=1}^{\infty}\cos\frac{x}{2^{n}},
\qquad 
\prod_{n=1}^{\infty}\cos\frac{x}{2^{n}}=\frac{\sin x}{x},
\]

one obtains  

\[
\prod_{k=1}^{\infty}\frac{\sin\!\left(\dfrac{\pi}{2^{k}}\right)}
{3\,\sin\!\left(\dfrac{\pi}{3\cdot2^{k}}\right)}
=
\prod_{m=2}^{\infty}
\Biggl[\frac{\cos\!\bigl(\dfrac{\pi}{2^{m}}\bigr)}
{\cos\!\bigl(\dfrac{\pi}{3\cdot2^{m}}\bigr)}\Biggr]^{\,m-1}.
\]

The two infinite products that appear are known and can be expressed
through the Glaisher–Kinkelin constant \(A\) :

\[
\prod_{m=2}^{\infty}\cos\!\Bigl(\frac{\pi}{2^{m}}\Bigr)^{\,m-1}
 = \frac{A^{3}}{2^{1/12}\,e^{1/8}\,\pi^{1/4}},\qquad
\prod_{m=2}^{\infty}\cos\!\Bigl(\frac{\pi}{3\cdot2^{m}}\Bigr)^{\,m-1}
 = \frac{A^{3}}{3^{1/12}\,e^{1/8}\,\pi^{1/4}} .
\]

Hence

\[
\prod_{k=1}^{\infty}\frac{\sin\!\left(\dfrac{\pi}{2^{k}}\right)}
{3\,\sin\!\left(\dfrac{\pi}{3\cdot2^{k}}\right)}
=
\frac{3^{1/12}}{2^{1/12}}
=
\boxed{\,\displaystyle\frac{3^{1/12}}{2^{1/12}}\;}
\]

and numerically

\[
\frac{3^{1/12}}{2^{1/12}}\approx 0.5888\; .
\]

